What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/cdma/pipe_id
Date:		August 2026
KernelVersion:	6.12
Contact:	Ciprian Marian Costea <ciprianmarian.costea@nxp.com>
Description:	(RW) IERB-authorized CDMA pipe identifier configured for this
		PCI function. Valid values are 0 through 255. The default is set
		by the default_pipe_id driver parameter and is 10 unless
		overridden.

		The value can be changed only while the device is inactive. Once
		the pipe is activated, writes fail with -EBUSY.

		The PCI BDF selects the hardware Station Interface exposed by
		firmware. Writing a pipe identifier does not change the SI assigned
		to the PCI function.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/cdma/activate
Date:		August 2026
KernelVersion:	6.12
Contact:	Ciprian Marian Costea <ciprianmarian.costea@nxp.com>
Description:	(WO) Activate the configured pipe and register its TX and RX
		character devices. Write 1, y, yes, true, or on to activate.

		Activation is one-way for the lifetime of the bound PCI device.
		Writing a false value returns -EINVAL. Repeating activation is a
		successful no-op. Runtime deactivation is intentionally unsupported
		because open file descriptors and asynchronous completions may still
		reference the pipe.

		On unbind the driver drains and flushes queued asynchronous
		completions before freeing the pipe. It does not, however,
		serialize against the synchronous read()/write() path: an
		in-flight blocking transfer is not force-drained, and closing a
		file descriptor does not wait for a syscall that is already
		mid-flight on it. Before unbinding the PCI function the
		user must therefore quiesce the pipe in userspace -
		close all pipe file descriptors and ensure no synchronous
		read()/write() is still in flight. Unbinding while a synchronous
		transfer is in progress is not supported.

		Firmware must authorize the selected pipe for the SI in PIDaAUR
		before the PCI function becomes visible to Linux.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/cdma/state
Date:		August 2026
KernelVersion:	6.12
Contact:	Ciprian Marian Costea <ciprianmarian.costea@nxp.com>
Description:	(RO) Current CDMA pipe state, configured pipe identifier, and PCI
		function. Example values are::

		  inactive pipe_id=10 pci=0000:01:00.2
		  active pipe_id=10 pci=0000:01:00.2

		Manual activation example::

		  DEV=/sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:01:00.2/cdma
		  echo 10 > $DEV/pipe_id
		  echo 1 > $DEV/activate
		  cat $DEV/state

		For a loadable driver, default_pipe_id, auto_activate, and
		auto_activate_bdf can be supplied to modprobe. For a built-in driver,
		the same parameters can be supplied on the kernel command line using
		the nxp-cdma driver-name prefix. Automatic activation requires an
		exact BDF so that other exposed CDMA functions remain inactive.

		Loadable driver example::

		  modprobe nxp-cdma default_pipe_id=10 auto_activate=1 \
		          auto_activate_bdf=0000:01:00.2

		Built-in driver kernel command-line example::

		  nxp-cdma.default_pipe_id=10 nxp-cdma.auto_activate=1 \
		  nxp-cdma.auto_activate_bdf=0000:01:00.2
